      "content": "If testing solenoids didn't reveal the issue and the behavior is more erratic than normal, it may indicate a more systemic problem. Internal transmission fault codes or filter clogs could also be causing the fluctuations. Additionally, faulty or worn-out microswitches or clutch pack components might also be contributing to the erratic behavior. Checking the transmission's relay and filter condition wouldn't hurt either.",
